      "message": "I was initially going to go in that direction, however can\u0027t there still be a race between setting the bool and draining?\n\nI.e. the BPF code is:\nif (!enabled) return\n// Fill in packet\n// Submit packet\n\nAnd the c++ code is:\n// Set bool to false\n// syncKernelRCU\n// Drain\n\nIn theory, the BPF code could be in the middle of filling while the c++ runs, and still insert into the ring buffer. Perhaps in practice it\u0027s a small enough gap/race that nothing would ever get through?\n\nI could also try draining before starting the poller, it\u0027s all mutex protected and a singleton, so unless something was very fast at starting then stopping, the drain should be reliable.",
